1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:04,797
Sonic-Log Action

2
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:10,910
Thank you.

3
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:01,720
Emergency alert!

4
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,040
Emergency alert!

5
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:05,418
Unknown ship spotted at 12 o 'clock!

6
00:02:05,580 --> 00:02:06,639
Are they bad guys?

7
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:08,620
They picked a bad time.

8
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:11,680
Well, they don't have a
single flag or sail up.

9
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:13,837
I don't know what kind of ship it is.

10
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:14,800
It's naked?

11
00:02:15,120 --> 00:02:16,657
Who would do that to their ship?

12
00:02:16,740 --> 00:02:18,637
What are they doing out here without sail?

13
00:02:18,720 --> 00:02:19,779
How should I know?

14
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:24,140
What's even weirder, the crew is
way too small for a ship that size.

15
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:28,037
Also, they look like they're
catatonic or something.

16
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:30,440
They're just sitting around in a daze.

17
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:37,480
Full speed! Sea monkeys!

18
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:39,030
Again?

19
00:02:39,113 --> 00:02:40,297
They must have followed us.

20
00:02:40,380 --> 00:02:41,920
Aw, crap, there's no wind!

21
00:02:42,020 --> 00:02:43,037
Hurry and throw us out!

22
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:44,440
Come on, start rowing!

23
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:49,877
What's wrong with them?

24
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:51,817
They're headed towards the sea monkeys.

25
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:54,253
That wave's going to swallow them whole.

26
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:55,250
Hey!

27
00:02:55,620 --> 00:02:56,580
Wake up!

28
00:02:57,080 --> 00:03:00,620
There's a giant wave filled
with sea monkeys! Turn around!

29
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:02,430
Huh?

30
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:04,060
A ship. Whoa.

31
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:07,760
It's a pirate ship. Come
on, man. On your feet.

32
00:03:07,900 --> 00:03:10,437
We've got to raid that ship
and swipe their treasure.

33
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:12,717
Wait, we're going to get
crushed by that giant wave.

34
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:14,337
Yeah, but we can't let them get away.

35
00:03:14,420 --> 00:03:15,479
Ready the cannons.

36
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:16,697
You ain't the boss.

37
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:17,610
Why don't you two?

38
00:03:17,693 --> 00:03:18,523
Turn!

39
00:03:18,606 --> 00:03:19,436
Somebody turn!

40
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:22,037
Wow, that's got to be the worst crew ever.

41
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:23,649
Forget about those idiots.

42
00:03:23,740 --> 00:03:25,377
They only want to steal our treasure.

43
00:03:25,460 --> 00:03:27,540
Which way do we turn? Who knows?

44
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:29,960
Where's the navigator? Give orders!

45
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:31,940
What navigator? Captain!

46
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:33,390
What captain?

47
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:37,510
What the?

48
00:03:37,593 --> 00:03:38,820
Who fired the cannon?

49
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:41,200
It's too late! We're going down!

50
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:43,820
You're a bunch of worthless morons!

51
00:03:44,100 --> 00:03:45,517
No, you're a bunch of morons!

52
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:46,659
What a stupid way!

53
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:10,020
At least it's calm.

54
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:13,817
Those gargantuan waves earlier were
actually caused by the sea monkeys.

55
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:16,777
The humidity and temperature seem
like they're pretty stable now.

56
00:04:16,860 --> 00:04:19,757
So we've got to be in the
next island's climate zone.

57
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:21,180
You hear that, Robin?

58
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:22,200
Any islands?

59
00:04:22,540 --> 00:04:24,457
We've been approaching
one for a while now.

60
00:04:24,540 --> 00:04:26,780
Why didn't you tell us?

61
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:29,497
Look, maybe tell us next
time you see an island.

62
00:04:29,580 --> 00:04:30,756
You know, like this.

63
00:04:30,980 --> 00:04:32,900
Land ahoy! Land!

64
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:34,240
I see land!

65
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:36,220
Yeah! Yeah!

66
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:38,160
Now you say it!

67
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:40,940
The fog looks pretty thick. Heavy fog?

68
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:42,101
That's not good.

69
00:04:42,740 --> 00:04:45,377
Hey, chopper, I need you
to stand forward watch.

70
00:04:45,460 --> 00:04:46,290
Right.

71
00:04:46,373 --> 00:04:50,597
Robin, do you have any idea how long
we've been waiting to see another island?

72
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:52,177
Sorry, won't happen again.

73
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:53,497
As long as you mean it.

74
00:04:53,580 --> 00:04:57,380
Okay, you know I can't stop
thinking about that ship.

75
00:04:57,660 --> 00:04:59,797
They didn't have a
captain or a navigator or

76
00:04:59,880 --> 00:05:02,497
even sails It was like
they had no idea what

77
00:05:02,580 --> 00:05:04,997
they were doing now What
kind of self-respecting

78
00:05:05,080 --> 00:05:06,997
pirates would head out to see like that?

79
00:05:07,080 --> 00:05:10,017
I'm guessing they got in a battle
and lost captain probably got

80
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:13,637
killed and then their ship got
plundered But that can't be yet.

81
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:15,157
I got a look at their ship.

82
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:17,897
It was in perfect condition
No signs of battle,

83
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:21,117
but it was still completely
stripped clean of anything a pirate

84
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:24,847
would need to survive They
probably weren't even pirates then.

85
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:26,860
Forget it. Mm.

86
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:30,497
They look like pirates to me,
crummy pirates, but still.

87
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:31,540
I don't know.

88
00:05:31,820 --> 00:05:34,291
I've got a bad feeling about this somehow.

89
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:35,677
Have you ever had a good one?

90
00:05:35,760 --> 00:05:37,819
Anyway, I wonder if there's a town.

91
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:39,057
I hope they got a shipyard.

92
00:05:39,140 --> 00:05:41,140
Reef, don't jump up right away.

93
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:49,560
I hope we can find a knowledgeable
shipwright to join us.

94
00:05:49,840 --> 00:05:51,317
Get the anchor ready!

95
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:52,840
We're near the shore!

96
00:05:54,180 --> 00:05:56,100
That feeling just got worse.

97
00:05:56,300 --> 00:06:00,418
Hey, Chopper, Usopp's come down with
another bout of scaredy-cat-itis.

98
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:02,344
Well, there's no care for that.

99
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:04,205
All right, let's go, let's go!

100
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:09,480
There's nothing at all!

101
00:06:10,420 --> 00:06:11,250
Ah!

102
00:06:11,333 --> 00:06:13,360
It's like a blank slate! It's cool!

103
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:15,880
All I can see is grass and trees!

104
00:06:17,860 --> 00:06:21,097
Man, this place is kind of depressing.

105
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:24,220
I wonder if anyone
actually lives here. Yahoo!

106
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:25,910
Hey!

107
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:35,700
Jeez, it's like they have no
concept of unknown danger.

108
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:40,360
You can see clear across the island,
and there's no threat in sight.

109
00:06:45,520 --> 00:06:47,440
You see something, Chopper?

110
00:06:51,180 --> 00:06:52,010
Hey!

111
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:55,110
Human?

112
00:06:55,380 --> 00:06:58,380
Have you ever seen a human
this furry and enormous?

113
00:06:58,480 --> 00:07:00,421
It's got to be some kind of bear!

114
00:07:02,560 --> 00:07:03,390
Whoa!

115
00:07:03,473 --> 00:07:04,480
It's so long!

116
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:06,060
It's a long bear!

117
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:07,900
I'm getting dizzy up here!

118
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:14,920
Hey, check out how long
this apple is! Whoa!

119
00:07:17,420 --> 00:07:20,420
I'm just realizing it, but
the trees are long, too!

120
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:29,195
Hey, look, is that a house over there?

121
00:07:30,540 --> 00:07:33,128
Yeah, I guess it kind
of looks like a house.

122
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:35,694
Let's go check it out.

123
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:45,360
Are you guys related? That's
a deer. I'm a reindeer.

124
00:08:00,540 --> 00:08:03,540
Everything on this island is so long!

125
00:08:04,740 --> 00:08:06,520
How did it get this way?

126
00:08:07,100 --> 00:08:08,600
Maybe it's the gravity?

127
00:08:09,340 --> 00:08:12,920
My body feels so stretched out
just from thinking about it!

128
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:16,160
What is a point in a place like this?

129
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:18,350
Hello?

130
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:19,530
Anyone home?

131
00:08:19,613 --> 00:08:20,457
What do you think you're doing?

132
00:08:20,540 --> 00:08:22,380
You can't go in there.

133
00:08:22,580 --> 00:08:24,937
For all we know, the boss of
the island lives in this house?

134
00:08:25,020 --> 00:08:27,217
And he's probably some
terrifyingly long man-snake?

135
00:08:27,300 --> 00:08:28,977
monster that'll swallow us whole.

136
00:08:29,060 --> 00:08:29,900
It's empty.

137
00:08:30,120 --> 00:08:31,680
No one's home. Huh?

138
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:34,520
Hey, Luffy, what's up?

139
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:36,237
There's a giraffe out here.

140
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:37,150
Really?

141
00:08:42,120 --> 00:08:42,950
Gah!

142
00:08:43,033 --> 00:08:44,725
Chopper, that's not a giraffe.

143
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:46,980
That's a horse with a long neck.

144
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:48,260
A long horse.

145
00:08:48,480 --> 00:08:49,360
Yeah, a horse?

146
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:52,740
Wow, what a pretty horse.

147
00:08:54,220 --> 00:08:56,691
She said thank you, and her name's Shelly.

148
00:08:56,800 --> 00:09:00,257
Going by the saddle she's got on
her, her owner must be close by.

149
00:09:00,340 --> 00:09:01,170
Huh?

150
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:03,266
Hey, what are you looking at?

151
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:04,840
Over there.

152
00:09:05,020 --> 00:09:07,777
There's something up with
those two bamboo trees.

153
00:09:07,860 --> 00:09:08,690
Huh?

154
00:09:09,060 --> 00:09:10,137
Yeah, you're right.

155
00:09:10,220 --> 00:09:11,161
Talk about tall.

156
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:12,880
I can't even see the top.

157
00:09:13,340 --> 00:09:15,120
That's not it. Look closer.

158
00:09:15,740 --> 00:09:16,740
Huh? Uh.

159
00:09:17,460 --> 00:09:18,290
Ah!

160
00:09:18,500 --> 00:09:19,382
They're moving!

161
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:23,080
They must be part of some wrong animal!

162
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:25,960
That pig's attacking Loopy!

163
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:27,560
Are you okay?

164
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:30,620
Get back here, Bamboo!

165
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:32,380
Be careful, Loopy!

166
00:09:32,760 --> 00:09:33,980
I'm not!

167
00:09:40,880 --> 00:09:43,080
All right! You did it!

168
00:09:43,740 --> 00:09:44,570
Yeah!

169
00:09:44,653 --> 00:09:45,483
I beat it!

170
00:09:45,566 --> 00:09:46,597
Why are you alone?

171
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:47,798
Where's your owner?

172
00:09:48,780 --> 00:09:50,380
You don't know where?

173
00:09:50,980 --> 00:09:52,840
That sounds awfully lonely.

174
00:09:57,860 --> 00:09:59,400
It might be bad guys.

175
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:01,020
Stay there and hide.

176
00:10:01,980 --> 00:10:03,300
What's going on?

177
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:10,540
Well, uh, I think that bamboo
tree was possessed by this spirit.

178
00:10:16,160 --> 00:10:17,520
Hey, what's the deal?

179
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:19,191
They blocked in our ship.

180
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:20,980
This can't be good.

181
00:10:21,740 --> 00:10:23,505
That's the ship I saw earlier.

182
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:26,160
You looking for a fight?

183
00:10:26,740 --> 00:10:29,034
Because we'll be happy to give you one.

184
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:32,520
We are the notorious Foxy Pirates!

185
00:10:32,740 --> 00:10:34,837
We want more than just a fight from you.

186
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:36,300
We want a showdown!

187
00:10:38,820 --> 00:10:41,020
A spirit? Well, yeah.

188
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:43,026
What else pops out of a tree?

189
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:46,260
Hey, can you speak?

190
00:10:48,820 --> 00:10:51,917
But acting like I don't
remember you, of course I do.

191
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:54,412
What have you been up to all these years?

192
00:10:54,580 --> 00:10:55,410
Huh?

193
00:10:55,493 --> 00:10:56,340
You guys know him?

194
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:58,580
Never seen him. Same here.

195
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:02,457
Ah, well, that would explain
why I don't remember you then.

196
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:03,677
Who are you, old man?

197
00:11:03,760 --> 00:11:05,054
And tell us the truth!

198
00:11:08,040 --> 00:11:09,981
If you want my name, it's Tonjit.

199
00:11:10,380 --> 00:11:13,086
But what I intend to
give you is my gratitude.

200
00:11:13,380 --> 00:11:16,577
I've been hoping someone would
knock me down off those stilts.

201
00:11:16,660 --> 00:11:17,490
Off what?

202
00:11:19,860 --> 00:11:22,157
Uh, oh, they are stilts.

203
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:24,937
We didn't realize because
they were so long.

204
00:11:25,020 --> 00:11:26,737
We couldn't even see you.

205
00:11:26,820 --> 00:11:30,477
I'm not surprised, I couldn't
even see the ground up there.

206
00:11:30,560 --> 00:11:34,677
So then, just to get this straight,
you're not a bamboo tree spirit?

207
00:11:34,760 --> 00:11:37,977
You're just an old guy whose stilts
I happen to think were attacking me!

208
00:11:38,060 --> 00:11:41,197
What were you doing walking
around on those stilts anyway?

209
00:11:41,280 --> 00:11:42,110
Well,

210
00:11:42,193 --> 00:11:45,897
I've always been a stilt enthusiast
So I decided to break some records

211
00:11:45,980 --> 00:11:50,057
and make the world's longest stilts
by using the bamboo on this island.

212
00:11:50,140 --> 00:11:52,557
I managed to get on them
with a little effort,

213
00:11:52,640 --> 00:11:54,717
but then I was too scared to climb down.

214
00:11:54,800 --> 00:11:56,117
That's just plain crazy.

215
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:58,200
I was up there ten years.

216
00:11:58,460 --> 00:11:59,440
Really crazy?

217
00:12:00,020 --> 00:12:02,897
Wait, you were up on those
stilts for ten whole years?

218
00:12:02,980 --> 00:12:07,537
That's right, and to make matters worse,
the bamboo kept growing the entire time.

219
00:12:07,620 --> 00:12:10,900
It just kept getting harder
and harder to climb down.

220
00:12:12,380 --> 00:12:13,420
So terrifying.

221
00:12:13,820 --> 00:12:16,114
How did you live up there for 10 years?

222
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:21,237
Well, most of the trees on this island are
just as tall as my stilts, if not taller.

223
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:23,379
So I was well fed from their fruit.

224
00:12:23,540 --> 00:12:25,877
He talks about it like it's no big deal.

225
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:27,489
10 long years of his life.

226
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:29,417
And speaking of stuff that's long,

227
00:12:29,500 --> 00:12:33,137
how come every living creature on
this island is so insanely long?

228
00:12:33,220 --> 00:12:36,517
It might seem crazy to an
outsider, but there is a reason.

229
00:12:36,600 --> 00:12:40,117
As I'm sure you've noticed, the
island is nothing but grass and trees.

230
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:44,220
It's dull, so everything grew long
out of a longing for excitement.

231
00:12:44,460 --> 00:12:45,960
He can't be serious.

232
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:47,812
You see that over there?

233
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:52,510
Platypus.

234
00:12:52,593 --> 00:12:53,960
You just said it longer.

235
00:12:54,220 --> 00:12:56,820
That one is a dachshund dog.

236
00:12:57,040 --> 00:12:59,760
And there are dangerous
animals as well. See?

237
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:02,160
Over there is a snow leopard.

238
00:13:02,380 --> 00:13:03,674
I'd steer clear of it.

239
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:08,229
Why is its head the
only thing that's long?

240
00:13:08,520 --> 00:13:09,497
I'm in your debt.

241
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:12,457
Come to my house and let me
show you some hospitality.

242
00:13:12,540 --> 00:13:14,900
Awesome! I'm starving! Me too!

243
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:17,937
Acustom in this village
to treat visitors to extra

244
00:13:18,020 --> 00:13:20,757
delicious milk from our
extra-long farm animals.

245
00:13:20,840 --> 00:13:21,670
Village?

246
00:13:21,753 --> 00:13:23,317
I didn't see any village out there.

247
00:13:23,400 --> 00:13:24,380
Or a farmhouse.

248
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:27,800
All the village is gone!

249
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:29,440
All our animals, too!

250
00:13:29,620 --> 00:13:30,837
You're nuts, old man.

251
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:34,157
I know it's been ten years, but
whole villages don't just disappear.

252
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:36,017
Yes, but this is a special case.

253
00:13:36,100 --> 00:13:40,220
I'll save the explanation until
after we've had a nice cool drink.

254
00:13:40,640 --> 00:13:43,640
I believe I've had some
milk tucked away somewhere.

255
00:13:45,380 --> 00:13:46,700
Did you say milk?

256
00:13:46,920 --> 00:13:50,685
You realize you were stuck on
those stilts for ten years, right?

257
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:56,637
I hope this cheese is to your liking.

258
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:57,757
You think we're stupid?

259
00:13:57,840 --> 00:14:00,957
You can't pass off your
disgusting old milk as cheese!

260
00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:03,217
If you don't want to eat
it, I won't force you.

261
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:05,997
But far be it from me, till
the cheese go to waste.

262
00:14:06,080 --> 00:14:08,597
Wait, so you're saying it's okay
to eat this stuff after all?

263
00:14:08,680 --> 00:14:10,151
Are you out of your mind?

264
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:11,656
What's the big deal?

265
00:14:11,880 --> 00:14:14,417
Some cheese tastes better
once it's finally aged.

266
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:17,137
Your high-stress lifestyles
have made your stomachs weak,

267
00:14:17,220 --> 00:14:20,937
whereas laid-back fellows such as
myself can eat whatever we like.

268
00:14:21,020 --> 00:14:25,667
You kids go on your fancy adventures,
but you're shy when it comes to new food.

269
00:14:28,060 --> 00:14:29,472
Someone call the doctor.

270
00:14:29,680 --> 00:14:31,457
What did you think was going to happen?

271
00:14:31,540 --> 00:14:32,370
Mara!

272
00:14:32,453 --> 00:14:33,283
No, no, no!

273
00:14:33,366 --> 00:14:34,196
Someone's going to die!

274
00:14:34,279 --> 00:14:35,109
Yeah, hurry!

275
00:14:35,192 --> 00:14:36,022
Wait, that's me!

276
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,240
It's food poisoning. Yeah, you think?

277
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:41,860
You're funny, old man.

278
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:44,030
You okay?

279
00:14:44,900 --> 00:14:49,547
Yes, excluding the fact that the entire
camp packed up and moved on without me.

280
00:14:49,700 --> 00:14:50,530
I see now.

281
00:14:50,720 --> 00:14:52,877
The village didn't disappear, it moved.

282
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:55,257
That must mean the people here are nomads.

283
00:14:55,340 --> 00:14:58,660
Indeed, and Long Ring Long
Land Island is our home.

284
00:14:58,980 --> 00:15:00,277
You are welcome here.

285
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:03,480
The island got its name
from its ring-like shape.

286
00:15:03,740 --> 00:15:05,837
Although it's technically one big circle,

287
00:15:05,920 --> 00:15:08,508
the tide's divided into
ten smaller islands.

288
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:12,197
You probably wouldn't guess that all
of the islands were actually connected,

289
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:13,221
but once a year,

290
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:14,777
when the tides are at their lowest,

291
00:15:14,860 --> 00:15:18,380
you can see Long Ring's true
form, if only for a few hours.

292
00:15:18,820 --> 00:15:22,997
We use this time to migrate from one
island to the next every three years,

293
00:15:23,080 --> 00:15:25,077
circling the ring again and again.

294
00:15:25,160 --> 00:15:28,937
Oh, so everyone moved to the next island
while you were stuck up in the trees.

295
00:15:29,020 --> 00:15:29,961
But rotten luck.

296
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:31,900
That's a good one!

297
00:15:32,100 --> 00:15:33,737
You're a real rebel, old man!

298
00:15:33,820 --> 00:15:35,857
If they stay on each
island for three years,

299
00:15:35,940 --> 00:15:39,637
then subtracting the ten years you spent
living on those stupid bamboo stilts?

300
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:41,537
it would still take a
good 20 years for them

301
00:15:41,620 --> 00:15:43,497
to come back around and
meet up with you again.

302
00:15:43,580 --> 00:15:46,957
Assuming you don't eat that cheese of
yours and die of food poisoning, of course.

303
00:15:47,040 --> 00:15:48,452
Well, it's sad but true.

304
00:15:48,580 --> 00:15:52,760
I just wish I had my
hoo-ros to ride again.

305
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:55,737
Then I could cross an island
every time the tides were

306
00:15:55,820 --> 00:15:59,232
low and catch up to the other
villages in only five years.

307
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:03,617
That's right they're the most graceful and

308
00:16:03,700 --> 00:16:06,257
beautiful animals on
the whole island once.

309
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:10,137
Tame they can be used to cross the
grassy plains with the greatest of ease.

310
00:16:10,220 --> 00:16:13,697
Without them it would be impossible
for our people to migrate.

311
00:16:13,780 --> 00:16:16,857
After all our belongings
are far too heavy to

312
00:16:16,940 --> 00:16:20,037
carry on our own and even
if we were strong enough

313
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:22,257
to move all our luggage
the tide would still

314
00:16:22,340 --> 00:16:24,577
rise and drown us before
we could make it across.

315
00:16:24,660 --> 00:16:26,657
Wouldn't it be easier
to take a boat instead?

316
00:16:26,740 --> 00:16:27,897
Yes of course.

317
00:16:27,980 --> 00:16:29,997
But unfortunately we
don't know how to sail.

318
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:33,297
And besides even if we were
able to charge a log post

319
00:16:33,380 --> 00:16:35,937
here that doesn't mean it
would point to the next island.

320
00:16:36,020 --> 00:16:40,097
The land may be split into ten pieces
but it's all part of the same place.

321
00:16:40,180 --> 00:16:42,677
Suppose I'll just have to wait 20 years.

322
00:16:42,760 --> 00:16:44,137
You'll be lonely.

323
00:16:44,220 --> 00:16:45,517
That's a long time.

324
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:52,437
Oh wait a second is a horse like a horse?

325
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:54,557
Hey I almost forgot about that.

326
00:16:54,640 --> 00:16:56,197
We saw a horse on the way here.

327
00:16:56,280 --> 00:17:02,877
Oh my sweet little Shelly you

328
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:04,437
waited for me all these years.

329
00:17:04,520 --> 00:17:06,637
You're such a pretty girl.

330
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:08,217
Look at you so cute.

331
00:17:08,300 --> 00:17:09,777
I missed you so much.

332
00:17:09,860 --> 00:17:12,417
You sure grown long since I've been away.

333
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:14,537
Oh you make me so proud.

334
00:17:14,620 --> 00:17:15,737
Good girl.

335
00:17:15,820 --> 00:17:16,957
That's a good girl.

336
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:19,817
I'm so sorry if you were.

337
00:17:19,900 --> 00:17:22,429
lonely while I was
gone, it's all my fault.

338
00:17:22,700 --> 00:17:24,980
I promise I'll never leave you again.

339
00:17:42,620 --> 00:17:44,040
What a pow, huh?

340
00:17:44,340 --> 00:17:47,657
Even though everyone else left, she's
still hung around all these years.

341
00:17:47,740 --> 00:17:49,480
That's my kind of horse.

342
00:17:49,900 --> 00:17:52,959
I don't know, it's one of
them is happier right now.

343
00:17:58,280 --> 00:18:00,400
Man, that horse sure is fast, huh?

344
00:18:00,560 --> 00:18:01,854
I want to ride it too.

345
00:18:02,300 --> 00:18:04,888
I see why that old man
likes horses so much.

346
00:18:05,060 --> 00:18:06,097
Now that I'm back,

347
00:18:06,180 --> 00:18:10,177
let's cross the sea together as
soon as the tide is low again, okay?

348
00:18:10,260 --> 00:18:14,637
You've waited through rainy days and
you've waited through snowy days as well.

349
00:18:14,720 --> 00:18:17,602
But from now on, we'll
have nothing but sunshine.

350
00:18:26,660 --> 00:18:30,177
Shelly, are you sure you won't
wait here for Tonjit all alone?

351
00:18:30,260 --> 00:18:32,157
We're taking all your friends with us.

352
00:18:32,240 --> 00:18:34,017
Please come with us, Shelly.

353
00:18:34,100 --> 00:18:37,377
We won't return to this
island for 27 years.

354
00:18:37,460 --> 00:18:41,401
You're going to be lonely if you
have to stay here all by yourself.

355
00:18:41,820 --> 00:18:43,937
We don't know where Tonjit ran off to.

356
00:18:44,020 --> 00:18:45,497
It's not worth waiting here.

357
00:18:45,580 --> 00:18:47,109
He might be gone for good.

358
00:18:47,740 --> 00:18:49,040
Girl, live well.

359
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:28,998
You know this old man's
afraid of heights, don't you?

360
00:20:02,520 --> 00:20:03,500
Oh, no!

361
00:20:03,800 --> 00:20:04,700
Are you okay?

362
00:20:14,960 --> 00:20:15,790
Shelly!

363
00:20:16,360 --> 00:20:17,500
What happened?

364
00:20:17,740 --> 00:20:19,200
We had a gunshot!

365
00:20:26,820 --> 00:20:28,180
Oh, this cat!

366
00:20:28,460 --> 00:20:29,740
Here, I'll get it!

367
00:20:33,980 --> 00:20:36,520
Sorry, suckers, but that horse is mine!

368
00:20:36,620 --> 00:20:37,957
Yeah, you tell him, boss.

369
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:39,922
Put those losers in their place.

370
00:20:40,500 --> 00:20:42,900
Whoever you are, you'll pay!

371
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:46,197
Whoever you are, you don't know?

372
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:48,620
My goodness, how rude.

373
00:20:52,760 --> 00:20:55,337
Don't tell me you've never
seen this face before!

374
00:20:55,420 --> 00:20:59,244
The only thing I know about your
face is that I'm gonna break it!

375
00:21:00,040 --> 00:21:01,560
He doesn't know me.

376
00:21:01,780 --> 00:21:03,597
Oh, no, don't get depressed, boss.

377
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:04,697
He's just saying that.

378
00:21:04,780 --> 00:21:05,610
It's a joke.

379
00:21:05,693 --> 00:21:07,037
Everybody knows who you are.

380
00:21:07,120 --> 00:21:09,414
Like you'd have any reason to know him.

381
00:21:10,220 --> 00:21:12,279
You're gonna make him cry, Hamburg!

382
00:21:12,460 --> 00:21:14,377
My name is Foxy.

383
00:21:14,460 --> 00:21:18,760
What's mine is mine, and
what's yours is mine too, Vivi!

384
00:21:18,880 --> 00:21:20,957
You should see the looks
on your dumb faces.

385
00:21:21,040 --> 00:21:23,817
What kind of pants he gets so
worked up over some stupid horse?

386
00:21:23,900 --> 00:21:27,077
If I didn't steal that thing myself,
then somebody else would do it!

387
00:21:27,160 --> 00:21:28,940
That's enough! Come, come!

388
00:21:30,400 --> 00:21:32,000
Hold it, Luffy, not yet!

389
00:21:33,360 --> 00:21:35,301
How'd you know my name was Luffy?

390
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:39,260
Because unlike some people,
we did our homework. Monkey D.

391
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:41,497
Luffy with a 100 million berry bounty.

392
00:21:41,580 --> 00:21:44,580
Roro Noah Zoro with a 60 million bounty.

393
00:21:44,840 --> 00:21:47,437
A lump of cash like that
is nothing to scoff at,

394
00:21:47,520 --> 00:21:50,577
especially considering that you
only have seven crew members.

395
00:21:50,660 --> 00:21:52,897
Now, with introductions out of the way,

396
00:21:52,980 --> 00:21:56,857
as captain of the Foxy Pirates, I challenge
you Straw Hats to a Daveyback fight!

397
00:21:56,940 --> 00:22:00,037
I don't know what that means, but
if you want to fight, bring it on!

398
00:22:00,120 --> 00:22:01,826
I'm sick of hearing you talk!

399
00:22:03,440 --> 00:22:05,037
Wait, now it all makes sense.

400
00:22:05,120 --> 00:22:06,977
I bet that messed up
crew we saw on the way

401
00:22:07,060 --> 00:22:08,797
here got challenged to a Daveyback fight,

402
00:22:08,880 --> 00:22:09,710
too!

403
00:22:11,780 --> 00:22:13,700
Which way do we turn? For those!

404
00:22:14,020 --> 00:22:16,160
Where's the Navigator? Give orders!

405
00:22:16,400 --> 00:22:17,282
What Navigator?

406
00:22:17,800 --> 00:22:19,400
Captain! The Captain!

407
00:22:20,620 --> 00:22:21,520
This is bad.

408
00:22:21,720 --> 00:22:24,000
I gotta stop him. Luffy, no!

409
00:22:24,720 --> 00:22:26,737
We're gonna end up losing our crew!

410
00:22:26,820 --> 00:22:28,257
What are you talking about, Usopp?

411
00:22:28,340 --> 00:22:31,737
I know this guy's a jerk, but
you can't agree to fight him!

412
00:22:31,820 --> 00:22:33,117
Hoi, hoi, hoi, hoi, hoi!

413
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:34,318
Feh, feh, feh, feh!

414
00:22:34,480 --> 00:22:35,580
Oh, too bad, kid.

415
00:22:35,780 --> 00:22:36,797
But don't take backs!

416
00:22:36,880 --> 00:22:38,417
You already agreed, remember?

417
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:39,977
Bring it on, I believe you said.

418
00:22:40,060 --> 00:22:41,580
Ain't that right Portia.

419
00:22:41,800 --> 00:22:45,497
Oh, that was definitely a bring it on
I heard and once you say bring it on.

420
00:22:45,580 --> 00:22:47,857
There's no turning back That's the rule.

421
00:22:47,940 --> 00:22:49,881
Should have kept your mouth shut.

422
00:22:51,460 --> 00:22:52,290
What's wrong?

423
00:22:52,373 --> 00:22:55,356
Don't tell me you aren't man
enough to keep your word!

424
00:22:56,760 --> 00:22:58,580
You're falling into a trap.

425
00:23:10,720 --> 00:23:13,200
Both of you step aside. Are you crazy?

426
00:23:15,240 --> 00:23:17,828
Shelly waited ten years
for me to come back.

427
00:23:18,060 --> 00:23:19,580
I won't let you take her.

428
00:23:19,720 --> 00:23:23,073
I know that you're angry, but
those are pirates, old man.

429
00:23:24,760 --> 00:23:26,777
You said the fight's already started?

430
00:23:26,860 --> 00:23:27,690
That's right.

431
00:23:27,773 --> 00:23:30,017
A Davyback fight begins
as soon as one captain

432
00:23:30,100 --> 00:23:31,997
accepts the challenge
from the other captain.

433
00:23:32,080 --> 00:23:32,940
No takebacks.

434
00:23:33,200 --> 00:23:36,737
In other words, your captain is fighting
our captain whether you like it or not.

435
00:23:36,820 --> 00:23:38,757
All you can do is sit
back and deal with it.

436
00:23:38,840 --> 00:23:40,040
I don't get this.

437
00:23:40,280 --> 00:23:42,437
If it's a fight, why do
I have to sit and wait?

438
00:23:42,520 --> 00:23:44,638
Let's do this right here, right now.

439
00:23:45,320 --> 00:23:46,937
You don't know anything, do you?

440
00:23:47,020 --> 00:23:48,077
It's not a real fight.

441
00:23:48,160 --> 00:23:51,748
It's more like a sports match
between different pirate crews.

442
00:23:52,120 --> 00:23:52,950
Exactly.

443
00:23:53,200 --> 00:23:56,737
Supposedly, the game originated in a
faraway place called Pirate Island.

444
00:23:56,820 --> 00:24:00,217
As the name implies, it's a sort
of secret paradise for pirates.

445
00:24:00,300 --> 00:24:01,130
At any rate,

446
00:24:01,213 --> 00:24:03,197
the main purpose of a
Davey-backed fight is to

447
00:24:03,280 --> 00:24:06,377
plunder desirable members
from another pirate's crew.

448
00:24:06,460 --> 00:24:08,860
Pirates plundering other pirates? Yes.

449
00:24:09,280 --> 00:24:12,515
No wonder your puny little
crew only has seven members.

450
00:24:12,600 --> 00:24:15,377
A Davy back fight is the best
way to pull in some new recruits.

451
00:24:15,460 --> 00:24:17,617
Since you're so clueless,
I'll tell you how it works.

452
00:24:17,700 --> 00:24:18,530
After each match,

453
00:24:18,613 --> 00:24:21,377
the winner can take any crew member
they want from the losing team.

454
00:24:21,460 --> 00:24:22,937
And once that person is chosen,

455
00:24:23,020 --> 00:24:26,317
they gotta pledge their undying loyalty
to their new captain on the spot.

456
00:24:26,400 --> 00:24:30,637
Both crews take their oath in the name
of Davy Jones, the Pirate of the Deep.

457
00:24:30,720 --> 00:24:33,140
So if you lose, you lose a crew member?

458
00:24:33,720 --> 00:24:35,680
Now you're getting it! Also,

459
00:24:36,100 --> 00:24:38,977
if the losing team doesn't have
any members worth plundering,

460
00:24:39,060 --> 00:24:44,001
the winning captain can add insult to injury
by robbing the ship of its Jolly Roger.

461
00:24:44,520 --> 00:24:48,177
So you're not just betting your crewmates,
but the pride of your ship, too.

462
00:24:48,260 --> 00:24:52,377
Winning might make you stronger, but
losing can leave you with nothing at all.

463
00:24:52,460 --> 00:24:54,237
You might as well be betting your life.

464
00:24:54,320 --> 00:24:55,150
I see.

465
00:24:55,300 --> 00:24:56,420
That explains it.

466
00:24:56,560 --> 00:24:59,560
That ship without a captain
or a navigator or sail.

467
00:24:59,680 --> 00:25:02,680
They must have lost everything
in a Davyback fight.

468
00:25:02,840 --> 00:25:06,677
Oh, so you saw the Fang Frog Pirates,
or what's left of them at least.

469
00:25:06,760 --> 00:25:10,137
How about we give you a chance to
admire our handiwork in person?

470
00:25:10,220 --> 00:25:13,577
Here, let's have a round of
applause for our brand new recruits!

471
00:25:13,660 --> 00:25:15,700
Long live the Foxy Pirates!

472
00:25:15,980 --> 00:25:19,177
Before I came here, I was the
captain of the Fang Frog Pirates.

473
00:25:19,260 --> 00:25:20,157
I was the doctor.

474
00:25:20,240 --> 00:25:21,500
I was the navigator.

475
00:25:21,600 --> 00:25:22,817
And I was the shipwright.

476
00:25:22,900 --> 00:25:25,637
We played five three-coin
games and lost them all.

477
00:25:25,720 --> 00:25:29,137
The captain, 13 crew members,
and our jolly Roger taken away.

478
00:25:29,220 --> 00:25:34,044
With so many people jumping ship, I guess
it was more like a merger than anything.

479
00:25:36,060 --> 00:25:37,437
You're nothing but scum.

480
00:25:37,520 --> 00:25:39,257
We're not playing your stupid game.

481
00:25:39,340 --> 00:25:40,170
Got it?

482
00:25:40,253 --> 00:25:42,017
There's no way we'd
ever sink to your level.

483
00:25:42,100 --> 00:25:45,417
You can say that all you want, but
it ain't the crew's decision to make.

484
00:25:45,500 --> 00:25:47,557
The Davyback fight begins the second one

485
00:25:47,640 --> 00:25:49,797
captain agrees to another
captain's challenge.

486
00:25:49,880 --> 00:25:50,939
What's the matter?

487
00:25:51,040 --> 00:25:52,697
Don't you have faith in your captain?

488
00:25:52,780 --> 00:25:55,117
If you don't agree with
the decisions he makes,

489
00:25:55,200 --> 00:25:57,847
maybe you're better off
joining us after all.

490
00:25:59,220 --> 00:26:01,044
Sorry, Nami, but they're right.

491
00:26:02,040 --> 00:26:05,777
All pirates take an unwritten oath to
follow their captain to the bitter end.

492
00:26:05,860 --> 00:26:10,213
If we turned our back on this fight
now, we'd be sailing away in disgrace.

493
00:26:10,420 --> 00:26:11,760
So? Who cares?

494
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:13,529
That's better than losing.

495
00:26:14,400 --> 00:26:17,694
Maybe for you, but I'd rather
die than live in disgrace.

496
00:26:18,500 --> 00:26:20,980
The same goes for me. Are you kidding?

497
00:26:21,140 --> 00:26:22,199
Get over yourself!

498
00:26:23,200 --> 00:26:24,760
You know how men can be.

499
00:26:24,940 --> 00:26:27,175
There's no point in arguing with them.

500
00:26:27,840 --> 00:26:29,977
I'll stop Luffy by force if I have to.

501
00:26:30,060 --> 00:26:31,897
Don't bother, it's too late!

502
00:26:31,980 --> 00:26:34,477
All that's left now is to
sit back and wait for the

503
00:26:34,560 --> 00:26:38,148
captains to fire a shot to signal
the beginning of the match.

504
00:26:42,220 --> 00:26:43,780
Oh, no way!

505
00:26:44,720 --> 00:26:46,017
Guess that settles it.

506
00:26:46,100 --> 00:26:47,629
Well, I'm not complaining.

507
00:26:48,220 --> 00:26:49,777
Should be interesting at least.

508
00:26:49,860 --> 00:26:53,000
He's agreed to the game. Yeah!

509
00:27:03,200 --> 00:27:05,820
Stupid! Stupid! Stupid! Stupid!

510
00:27:06,140 --> 00:27:07,375
Why didn't you agree?

511
00:27:07,520 --> 00:27:08,977
You could end up losing your crew!

512
00:27:09,060 --> 00:27:10,160
You could lose me!

513
00:27:10,420 --> 00:27:12,160
Oh, I'm gonna win this thing!

514
00:27:12,900 --> 00:27:15,860
Now the Davey Mac fight
is officially underway!

515
00:27:16,380 --> 00:27:17,210
Good!

516
00:27:17,293 --> 00:27:19,864
The sooner I can pound
your face in, the better!

517
00:27:20,440 --> 00:27:21,857
I'd like to see you try!

518
00:27:21,940 --> 00:27:24,420
All right, bring it on, split-head!

519
00:27:24,680 --> 00:27:26,327
He doesn't like my hair cut.

520
00:27:26,540 --> 00:27:28,220
That's not true! Hey!

521
00:27:28,700 --> 00:27:29,617
Apologize to him!

522
00:27:29,700 --> 00:27:31,557
Our boss is sensitive about his looks!

523
00:27:31,640 --> 00:27:33,337
He's sensitive about everything.

524
00:27:33,420 --> 00:27:34,949
He's got a heart of glass.

525
00:27:36,460 --> 00:27:38,397
How many times do I have to tell you?

526
00:27:38,480 --> 00:27:39,310
Don't laugh!

527
00:27:39,800 --> 00:27:40,630
Luffy,

528
00:27:40,713 --> 00:27:44,737
now listen, I'm as angry about the old
guy's horse as you are, but this is madness!

529
00:27:44,820 --> 00:27:45,650
Good!

530
00:27:45,733 --> 00:27:46,737
Use that anger to thrash us!

531
00:27:46,820 --> 00:27:47,697
What are you doing up?

532
00:27:47,780 --> 00:27:48,797
I thought you hurt your back!

533
00:27:48,880 --> 00:27:49,762
Leave it to me!

534
00:27:54,060 --> 00:27:56,413
You don't know what you're getting into.

535
00:28:00,880 --> 00:28:01,897
Sausage on the stick!

536
00:28:01,980 --> 00:28:03,197
Get your sausage on the stick!

537
00:28:03,280 --> 00:28:07,897
We got wrong, we got cheeseburgers,
turkey legs, yaki Sabo, we got it all.

538
00:28:07,980 --> 00:28:10,340
It's time for the opening ceremonies.

539
00:28:12,340 --> 00:28:13,170
You Spear down.

540
00:28:13,253 --> 00:28:14,083
Shut up.

541
00:28:14,166 --> 00:28:15,780
Come on, let's hear the odds.

542
00:28:15,940 --> 00:28:17,920
All competitors, get ready.

543
00:28:18,060 --> 00:28:20,737
Split Head may be a jerk, but
he sure knows how to party.

544
00:28:20,820 --> 00:28:22,437
And check out all the people he invited.

545
00:28:22,520 --> 00:28:23,350
Is that his crew?

546
00:28:23,433 --> 00:28:24,720
Wow, there's so many.

547
00:28:25,800 --> 00:28:27,660
Five jumbo yaki sobas, please.

548
00:28:28,600 --> 00:28:30,188
Whose side are you on, huh?

549
00:28:31,520 --> 00:28:33,300
Now, let's calm down, boys.

550
00:28:33,420 --> 00:28:34,417
We're about to stop.

551
00:28:34,500 --> 00:28:36,577
I love you, Portia! Marry me!

552
00:28:36,660 --> 00:28:39,057
Since our challengers have
never played this game before,

553
00:28:39,140 --> 00:28:40,905
let's go over the rules, okay?

554
00:28:41,120 --> 00:28:43,457
First of all, whatever you
lose in one of the matches,

555
00:28:43,540 --> 00:28:45,237
whether it's your crew, your Jolly Roger,

556
00:28:45,320 --> 00:28:46,177
or anything else,

557
00:28:46,260 --> 00:28:50,319
the only way you can take it back
is with another daily-backed fight.

558
00:28:50,840 --> 00:28:51,670
Second,

559
00:28:51,753 --> 00:28:53,397
any crew member taken
by the winner must swear

560
00:28:53,480 --> 00:28:56,097
undying loyalty to their
new captain on the spot.

561
00:28:56,180 --> 00:28:57,010
No exceptions.

562
00:28:57,520 --> 00:29:02,800
Third, if your Jolly Roger is taken, you
can't ever fly it again. Never ever. Mommy!

563
00:29:03,120 --> 00:29:04,767
I got you some cotton candy!

564
00:29:04,900 --> 00:29:08,488
I don't know how everyone can
be so calm at a time like this.

565
00:29:09,400 --> 00:29:12,497
That's already settled, so you
might as well stop complaining.

566
00:29:12,580 --> 00:29:13,410
Finally,

567
00:29:13,493 --> 00:29:15,017
if you happen to break any of these rules,

568
00:29:15,100 --> 00:29:17,917
you'll be labeled a disgrace to
all pirates and banished to D .B.

569
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:18,830
Jones' locker.

570
00:29:18,913 --> 00:29:20,684
So do you swear to uphold them?

571
00:29:21,200 --> 00:29:22,500
I swear! I swear!

572
00:29:27,940 --> 00:29:29,020
Then it's settled.

573
00:29:29,420 --> 00:29:32,300
Three coins, three games, orthodox rules.

574
00:29:32,740 --> 00:29:35,320
Let David Jones be our witness.

575
00:29:42,140 --> 00:29:42,970
Huh?

576
00:29:43,053 --> 00:29:44,645
So who's this David Jones guy?

577
00:29:44,880 --> 00:29:47,437
A pirate who was cursed
by the devil and forced

578
00:29:47,520 --> 00:29:49,957
to spend all of eternity
at the bottom of the sea.

579
00:29:50,040 --> 00:29:52,197
I've never heard of
people living underwater.

580
00:29:52,280 --> 00:29:53,837
Well, that's what the legend says.

581
00:29:53,920 --> 00:29:57,677
And all the ships and treasures that
sink beneath the waves go to his locker,

582
00:29:57,760 --> 00:29:59,701
never to be seen by anyone again.

583
00:30:00,140 --> 00:30:02,787
I knew the ocean was
scary, but that's crazy.

584
00:30:03,580 --> 00:30:04,410
Yummy.

585
00:30:04,493 --> 00:30:06,297
Davy Jones has been
taking his picks from all

586
00:30:06,380 --> 00:30:08,937
sorts of pirates for as
long as anyone can remember.

587
00:30:09,020 --> 00:30:11,657
That's why we call it a
Davy-backed fight in honor of

588
00:30:11,740 --> 00:30:14,975
the pirate that may someday
claim your crew is his own.

589
00:30:15,840 --> 00:30:16,670
A captain,

590
00:30:16,940 --> 00:30:21,352
a swordsman, a navigator, a sniper, a
cook, a doctor, and an archaeologist.

591
00:30:22,240 --> 00:30:25,887
So tough, but I do have to decide
who it is I'm going to take.

592
00:30:26,100 --> 00:30:28,453
I believe it to be that one right there.

593
00:30:30,680 --> 00:30:31,620
You jerk.

594
00:30:31,920 --> 00:30:34,540
You've landed us in a real mess, Loopy.

595
00:30:34,820 --> 00:30:36,060
What's the big deal?

596
00:30:36,160 --> 00:30:37,513
All we gotta do is win.

597
00:30:37,780 --> 00:30:39,417
You're forgetting something.

598
00:30:39,500 --> 00:30:41,618
You gotta fill out your team roster.

599
00:30:41,720 --> 00:30:43,426
Our party organizer needs it.

600
00:30:43,660 --> 00:30:46,836
And once you've picked your
lineup, it's set in stone.

601
00:30:47,600 --> 00:30:49,420
We can't lose this thing.

602
00:30:49,580 --> 00:30:52,657
I just know they're gonna
take Captain Usopp if we do.

603
00:30:52,740 --> 00:30:53,800
No, they aren't.

604
00:30:53,940 --> 00:30:55,234
They're gonna take me.

605
00:30:55,500 --> 00:30:56,640
I'm the cute one.

606
00:30:56,920 --> 00:30:59,380
And it's time to announce the rosters.

607
00:30:59,540 --> 00:31:02,277
Each team has chosen to
represent them in today's events.

608
00:31:02,360 --> 00:31:04,857
Because I got a disease that
prevents me from racing.

609
00:31:04,940 --> 00:31:07,957
I don't want to do this stupid
race either, so just man out.

610
00:31:08,040 --> 00:31:09,452
Better not slow me down.

611
00:31:09,640 --> 00:31:10,699
Right back at you.

612
00:31:10,880 --> 00:31:13,660
I'm going to try and hide it.

613
00:31:14,920 --> 00:31:17,100
Oh, who cares? Let's go.

614
00:31:17,880 --> 00:31:19,480
I am Ikaminizu.

615
00:31:19,720 --> 00:31:22,417
You may know me as the Foxy
Pirates party organizer,

616
00:31:22,500 --> 00:31:24,517
but today I will be your commentator.

617
00:31:24,600 --> 00:31:28,600
Our first event of the day
is round one, the Donut Race.

618
00:31:29,700 --> 00:31:32,117
Legal boats for the Donut Race can only be

619
00:31:32,200 --> 00:31:34,897
constructed from two oars
and three empty barrels.

620
00:31:34,980 --> 00:31:37,877
You will be disqualified if
you use any other materials.

621
00:31:37,960 --> 00:31:41,195
This is the perfect chance
for shipwrights to show off.

622
00:31:42,880 --> 00:31:44,900
And time is just about up.

623
00:31:45,020 --> 00:31:46,660
I hope everyone is ready.

624
00:31:47,060 --> 00:31:52,197
It's the Straw Hat team of Navigator Nami,
Sniper Usopp, and Archaeologist Robin.

625
00:31:52,280 --> 00:31:54,820
Their official craft is the Beryl Tiger!

626
00:31:55,480 --> 00:31:58,340
That chick with the orange
hair is smokin' hot.

627
00:31:58,480 --> 00:32:01,557
I am praying that the
dark-haired babe joins our crew.

628
00:32:01,640 --> 00:32:02,777
They can keep the guy.

629
00:32:02,860 --> 00:32:03,690
Yeah, agreed.

630
00:32:04,240 --> 00:32:05,070
Ooh!

631
00:32:05,153 --> 00:32:06,057
Gather round, folks!

632
00:32:06,140 --> 00:32:07,611
The final haunts are end!

633
00:32:07,960 --> 00:32:09,019
Just as I thought!

634
00:32:09,120 --> 00:32:12,900
The top spot goes to our idle
and fellow foxy pirate, Parcha!

635
00:32:13,200 --> 00:32:15,000
Oh, you're too kind!

636
00:32:15,540 --> 00:32:17,857
Joining her is the Fishman Capote!

637
00:32:17,940 --> 00:32:22,300
Their vessel is the cutie wagon
led by the star shark, Mom-Nah.

638
00:32:23,900 --> 00:32:26,520
Yeah, take him down,
Portia, you can do it.

639
00:32:27,000 --> 00:32:29,597
Hold on, you've got a
shark pool in your boat?

640
00:32:29,680 --> 00:32:32,957
I didn't hear him mention any
rules forbidding the use of sharks.

641
00:32:33,040 --> 00:32:35,677
I'll continue to provide
commentary throughout the race?

642
00:32:35,760 --> 00:32:38,597
with a bird's eye view of the
action from atop Chirp Chirp,

643
00:32:38,680 --> 00:32:40,562
a rare South Blue Super Sparrow.

644
00:32:41,420 --> 00:32:42,380
Chirp Chirp!

645
00:32:42,660 --> 00:32:44,017
You're sure this won't sink?

646
00:32:44,100 --> 00:32:46,937
I told you, I am not a
professional shipwright, OK?

647
00:32:47,020 --> 00:32:49,920
Now, on your marks!
